Actually, let me restructure the per-file scoring into a pure function that both the loop and the test use. The loop currently computes score inline. I'll extract:

```rust
/// Pure per-file score combination: weighted signal sum + test-density penalty
/// + mutation-survival term + recency bump. Separated from
/// `compute_file_risk_scores` so the recency-vs-historical calibration can be
/// unit-tested with deterministic synthetic inputs.
fn combine_risk_score(
    signals: &[f64; 7],  // normalized, in RISK_WEIGHTS order
    weights: &[f64; 7],
    tests_per_100: f64,
    path_is_rs: bool,
    mutation_survival: f64,
    touched_recently: bool,
) -> f64 {
    let mut score = signals.iter().zip(weights.iter()).map(|(s, w)| s * w).sum::<f64>();

    if path_is_rs {
        score += f64::max(0.0, (5.0 - tests_per_100) * 2.0) / 100.0;
    }
    if mutation_survival > 0.0 {
        score += MUTATION_WEIGHT * mutation_survival;
    }
    if touched_recently {
        score += RECENCY_BUMP;
    }
    score
}
```

